    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2 tests, 0 failures/errors).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `membershipTier` field on the owner response.\n\nThe `GET /api/owners/{id}` response body is generated from `openapi.yml` into `OwnerDto` and populated by MapStruct, with derived fields (`displayName`, `membershipNumber`, etc.) computed via `@Mapping` expressions. `membershipTier` fits the same pattern, since both inputs it needs are already stored on `Owner`:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `membershipTier` (string, read-only) property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a mapping expression:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"membershipTier\",\n       expression = \"java(owner.getNamesakeCount() != null && owner.getNamesakeCount() == 0 \"\n           + \"&& owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank() ? \\\"SILVER\\\" : \\\"BRONZE\\\")\")\n   ```\n   Returns `SILVER` when `namesakeCount == 0` and an email is present, otherwise `BRONZE`. `namesakeCount` is set by the existing `CountNamesakes` step during create; email is normalized/stored by `NormalizeOwnerEmail`. Null-guards keep it safe if either is absent (\u2192 `BRONZE`).\n\nNo new function classes or YAML were needed \u2014 this is a derived response field, so it belongs in the response mapper rather than the OfficeFloor pipeline.",
